---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const updated = '2026-06-04';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use — HomeMaterialCalc.com"
  description="Terms of use for HomeMaterialCalc.com. Read before using our free material estimator calculators."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-brand-600">Home</a> › <span class="text-gray-700">Terms of Use</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">

      <h2>Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing and using HomeMaterialCalc.com ("the Site"), you accept and agree to be
        bound by these Terms of Use. If you do not agree to these terms, please do not use the Site.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of Calculators — Estimates Only</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>All results provided by our calculators are estimates for planning purposes only.</strong>
        While we make every effort to ensure the accuracy of our formulas and material constants,
        actual material quantities may vary due to:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Variations in material density by product, brand, region, and moisture content</li>
        <li>Measurement inaccuracies in your project dimensions</li>
        <li>Site-specific conditions such as uneven ground, compaction, or settling</li>
        <li>Differences between pallet sizes or bag yields from specific suppliers</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <strong>Always confirm final quantities with your local supplier before ordering.</strong>
        For large or structural projects, consult a qualified professional.
      </p>

      <h2>No Professional Advice</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing on this Site constitutes professional engineering, construction, landscaping,
        or other professional advice. The calculators are general-purpose estimating tools for
        DIY homeowners. For structural concrete, load-bearing applications, or projects with
        safety implications, hire a licensed professional.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        The content, design, and code of this Site are owned by HomeMaterialCalc.com.
        You may use the calculators and reference the information for personal, non-commercial
        purposes. Reproduction, redistribution, or commercial use of site content without
        written permission is prohibited.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        This Site displays advertisements through Google AdSense. These ads are provided by
        Google and may be targeted based on your browsing behavior. We are not responsible for
        the content or accuracy of third-party advertisements.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        HomeMaterialCalc.com and its operators shall not be liable for any direct, indirect,
        incidental, special, or consequential damages arising from your use of the Site or
        reliance on any calculator results. Use this Site at your own risk.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        We strive for accuracy and document our sources on the <a href="/methodology" class="text-brand-600">Methodology page</a>.
        Material constants are industry averages and may not match every specific product.
        If you discover an error, please <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-600">contact us</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We reserve the right to update these terms at any time. Continued use of the Site
        after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the United States. Any disputes shall be
        resolved in accordance with applicable US law.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-600">Contact us</a>.
      </p>

    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
